{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_bryq7tekysoy33xx7cv4u4oeb7fwui5lmsauiutfvwen4zuesk2q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Verification complete — the Rust translation is bit-identical to the C, no fixes were needed.**\n\nThe library is tiny (one TU, one exported function `float contrast_ratio(cb_rgb_255, cb_rgb_255)`), so I verified it exhaustively rather than by sampling.\n\n| Gate | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `cargo check` | clean, 0 errors |\n| C `.so` built (CMake) | `c_src/build/libharvest-work-0mZzK9.so` |\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | C exports `contrast_ratio` only; Rust `.so` exports it identically. Symbol diff = ∅, 0 undefined non-libc syms (both import libm `pow`). Rust correctly does *not* export the C-`static` helpers. |\n| `CONFIGS.md` — Phase B | 76 rows, all [x]. Rows 1–64 = full cross product of the per-channel sRGB-transfer branch masks (`X > 0.04045` ⇒ byte ≤10 linear / ≥11 `pow`) for both colours × both argument orders (the `High < Low` swap), 256 seeded-random samples each; rows 65–76 = exhaustive grey×grey (65 536 pairs), per-channel sweeps, threshold and top-of-range boundary sweeps, `A == B`, 200 000 random full-range pairs, extreme ratios, order symmetry, register-padding independence. |\n| Extra closure | `contrast_ratio` factors through `cbLuminance`, which has only 256³ inputs — so I ran **all 16 777 216 colours × 3 references (≈50M FFI call pairs)** and every result matched bit-for-bit. |\n| `ERRORS.md` — Phase C | 10 rows, all with passing tests. The C has **no** error returns, asserts, range checks, pointers, lengths or enums — its rejection surface is entirely IEEE degenerates: `+inf` (`0x7F800000`) for divide-by-zero-luminance in both argument orders, quiet `NaN` (identical payload) for black/black, exactly `1.0f` for equal inputs, plus wide-int-truncation and padding-byte cases through the ABI. All asserted on raw `u32` bits, not \"both failed\". |\n| Binary driver | none — the project builds only a shared library. |\n| Feature combinations | `Cargo.toml` declares **no `[features]`**; suite passes under default and `--no-default-features`. Also re-ran the whole suite against C at `-O0`, `-O2`, `-O3` and CMake defaults, and against both the debug and release Rust `cdylib` — 22/22 tests pass in every configuration. |\n\nKey correctness details the Rust already gets right: the ternary is evaluated in `double` (float operands promoted by the `0.04045`/`0.055`/`1.055`/`12.92` literals) then cast back to `float`; the luminance dot product accumulates in single precision left-to-right; the Rust binds the *platform* `pow` via `extern \"C\"` instead of Rust's own, which is what makes the `pow` arm bit-exact; and the missing WCAG `+0.05` offset plus the unguarded `High / Low` are faithfully preserved rather than \"fixed\".\n\nFiles added: `translation/SYMBOLS.md`, `translation/ERRORS.md`, `translation/CONFIGS.md`, `translation/tests/differential.rs`; `libloading = \"0.8\"` added to `[dev-dependencies]`. Nothing in `c_src/` was modified.\n\nTwo notes: crates.io is blocked by the sandbox proxy, so cargo commands need `--offline` (`libloading 0.8.9` was already in the local registry cache). And the tests load the *release* `cdylib` by default, so run `cargo build --release --offline` before `cargo test --release --offline`; `DIFF_C_SO` / `DIFF_RUST_SO` override either library path."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2982,"cache_read_input_tokens":54200,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2982,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8349b5e6-8011-4ce3-8d5e-ff558e066657","uuid":"43728108-0606-4527-9bac-ecfbe38414ce","timestamp":"2026-09-05T00:00:56.774Z"}
